			"notes": "# Hidder 3.0.0\n\nHidder 3.0.0 is the Fabric client companion for [ModSeeker 3.0.0](https://github.com/RAFIN-G/ModSeeker/releases/tag/v3.0.0). **Update both projects together.** A v2 client does not complete v3 verification.\n\n## In this release\n\n- Each Minecraft-specific JAR supports Fabric Loader **0.19.3, 0.19.5 and 0.20.1**. You do not need a separate Hidder download for each of these Loader versions.\n- Updated native verification and class-integrity checks support the v3 report protocol.\n- Reports include mod IDs and versions, including declared bundled mods. Advanced verification also reports file hashes; launcher identification responds to the server's launcher challenge.\n- Mod reports are signed and encrypted for the connected server. Verification runs automatically when you join.\n- The Windows native library is bundled. Players do not need a separate OpenSSL installation, C++ runtime installer, service or virtual machine.\n\n## Choose your download\n\n**Windows x64 only.** macOS, Linux, Windows ARM and Android/iOS Java launchers are not supported. Use Fabric and install Fabric API for the same Minecraft version.\n\nDownload **one** matching Hidder JAR:\n\n| Minecraft | Java | File |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1.21 | 21 | `hidder-3.0.0+mc1.21.jar` |\n| 1.21.4 | 21 | `hidder-3.0.0+mc1.21.4.jar` |\n| 1.21.7 | 21 | `hidder-3.0.0+mc1.21.7.jar` |\n| 1.21.8 | 21 | `hidder-3.0.0+mc1.21.8.jar` |\n| 1.21.9 | 21 | `hidder-3.0.0+mc1.21.9.jar` |\n| 1.21.10 | 21 | `hidder-3.0.0+mc1.21.10.jar` |\n| 1.21.11 | 21 | `hidder-3.0.0+mc1.21.11.jar` |\n| **26.1.2** | 25 | `hidder-3.0.0+mc26.1.jar` |\n| 26.2 | 25 | `hidder-3.0.0+mc26.2.jar` |\n| 26.3 | 25 | `hidder-3.0.0+mc26.3.jar` |\n\nThe filename labelled `mc26.1` targets **26.1.2**, not 26.1 or 26.1.1. Other Fabric Loader versions are not supported by this release. Fabric Loader and Fabric API are separate dependencies.\n\n## Installing or updating\n\n1. Select the correct Minecraft version and Fabric Loader 0.19.3, 0.19.5 or 0.20.1 in your launcher.\n2. Put the matching Hidder JAR and Fabric API in that instance's `mods/` folder. Remove the older Hidder JAR.\n3. Launch Minecraft with the Java version shown above and join a server running ModSeeker 3.0.0.\n\nServer owners choose which mods and launchers are allowed. If the server rejects your setup, read the disconnect message or contact its administrator.\n\n## What is reported\n\nHidder sends the requested reports through your existing Minecraft connection to the server you join. Server administrators can read them. It does not upload mod JAR contents, local paths, hardware IDs, resource packs or shader packs, and it does not use a separate telemetry service.\n\nSee the [data description](https://github.com/RAFIN-G/Hidder#what-hidder-sends) for the report fields and when they are sent.\n\n## Verification files\n\nThe downloads include `official-release-manifest.json`, its `.minisig` signature and `official-release.minisign.pub`. To check an individual JAR, first verify the manifest signature with a trusted publisher public key, then compare the JAR's SHA-256 with its entry in that signed manifest. You do not need the other builds to check your chosen download.\n\nPublisher public-key SHA-256 (raw key):\n\n```text\nbd58f8232d4dde40dc4cb2c04c0c4d6c44e06ca76371c092290828eddbe8679d\n```\n\nGitHub's automatic source archives contain source code, not a ready-to-install mod.\n\n[Installation](https://github.com/RAFIN-G/ModSeeker/wiki/Installation-and-Compatibility) · [Troubleshooting](https://github.com/RAFIN-G/ModSeeker/wiki/Troubleshooting) · [FAQ](https://github.com/RAFIN-G/ModSeeker/wiki/FAQ-and-Support)"
		},
